[
  {
    "title": "ARCS: Kaiora Point survey ledger, 1887 entries",
    "create_time": 1719000000.0,
    "update_time": 1719000188.0,
    "mapping": {
      "root-arcs-0001-ledger": {
        "id": "root-arcs-0001-ledger",
        "message": null,
        "parent": null,
        "children": [
          "arcs-0001-ledger-n01"
        ]
      },
      "arcs-0001-ledger-n01": {
        "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n01",
        "message": {
          "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n01",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1719000047.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I have a photograph of a ledger page from the Kaiora Point survey. The heading reads “Survey of the Kaiora Point reserve, commenced 14 March 1887”. Below it there are three columns: chain, bearing, remarks. The first row says 12 chains, N 47° E, “to the karaka stand”. What would 'chains' mean here?"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {
            "attachments": [
              {
                "id": "file-KP1887a",
                "name": "kaiora-ledger-p14.jpg",
                "size": 2841204,
                "mime_type": "image/jpeg"
              }
            ]
          },
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "root-arcs-0001-ledger",
        "children": [
          "arcs-0001-ledger-n02"
        ]
      },
      "arcs-0001-ledger-n02": {
        "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n02",
        "message": {
          "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n02",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1719000094.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "A chain is a surveyor's unit of 66 feet (20.1168 m), so 12 chains is 792 feet or about 241.4 metres. A bearing of N 47° E is measured clockwise from magnetic north unless the ledger states a true-north correction. “To the karaka stand” is a natural monument call: the line was run until it met a stand of karaka trees, which means the boundary was fixed to a living feature rather than a fixed mark."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": true,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {
            "model_slug": "gpt-4o"
          },
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "arcs-0001-ledger-n01",
        "children": [
          "arcs-0001-ledger-n03",
          "arcs-0001-ledger-branch"
        ]
      },
      "arcs-0001-ledger-n03": {
        "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n03",
        "message": {
          "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n03",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1719000141.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The second row is harder to read. It looks like '8 ch 50 lk' and the remark is 'to the old pa fence line'. Date in the margin is 16 March 1887."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {},
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "arcs-0001-ledger-n02",
        "children": [
          "arcs-0001-ledger-n04"
        ]
      },
      "arcs-0001-ledger-n04": {
        "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n04",
        "message": {
          "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-n04",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1719000188.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "8 chains 50 links is 8.5 chains, 561 feet, roughly 171.0 metres (100 links to the chain). The remark places the line at a pa fence — a fortified site boundary — which is significant: in 1887 surveyors frequently recorded pa earthworks as monuments precisely because they were visible and long-standing. If the ledger is the only surviving record of that fence line, it is evidence of the pa's extent at that date."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": true,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {
            "model_slug": "gpt-4o",
            "citations": [
              {
                "metadata": {
                  "title": "Survey regulations 1878",
                  "url": "https://example.invalid/survey-regs-1878"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "recipient": "all"
        },
        "parent": "arcs-0001-ledger-n03",
        "children": []
      },
      "arcs-0001-ledger-branch": {
        "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-branch",
        "message": {
          "id": "arcs-0001-ledger-branch",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1719000020.0,
          "update_time": null,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The second row is hard to read — possibly '8 ch 50 lk'? [edited]"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
          "weight": 1.0,
          "metadata": {
            "is_edited_branch": true
          },
          "recipient": "all"
        },
